aming at the dragon would hurt it in  some way  now i don't know about you but that  might be one of the dumbest things i've  ever heard  i wish i was making it up but there were  a large number of fans who really  thought that  i actually think i have the right answer  the reason why i want to share this  is because i still see fans discussing  this scene in some of the facebook  groups  i haven't seen anyone else look at this  scene the same way that i do  now normally i would not say something  like this but in this case  i believe almost everyone is looking at  this scene the wrong way  now let me explain why i think jon snow  screamed in viserion's face  the first thing we need to do is go back  and look at where this scene actually  started  what really set this in motion is when  jon and the night king had their final  face-to-face meeting  if you remember this was right after  daenerys set the night king on fire with  drogon  after daenerys realized it did not work  the night king grabbed another spear  then daenerys flew off leaving jon snow  there to face the night king  unfortunately we did not see them fight  one versus one  this is when the night king did what he  always does he lifted his arms  raising the dead all around john as soon  as jon was surrounded  the night king walked off heading  directly for the godswood  now in that moment jon knew he was  screwed  not only was he now surrounded by  hundreds if not thousands of whites  but the night king essentially had a  direct line for the godswood  jon knew that he had to work as fast as  he could if he was going to save  everyone  he knew he could not allow the night  king to get to the godswood before he  did  that was when the desperation really set  in because he could see the night king  heading that way  he knew the night king would be in the  godswood in the matter of moments  now luckily for jon danny did not go far  she doubled back  and burned a lot of the whites who were  stopping jon from moving forward  as soon as she did that jon looked at  her and yelled bran  then dany yelled go because she also  knew that the night king was heading  that way  fast as jon makes his way through  winterfell fighting off the dead one by  one  this is where we really saw how  desperate he was this is when jon  finally made it inside winterfell's  courtyard  leaving him only about a hundred yards  away from the night king  and ultimately bran all jon had to do  now  was make it to the other side he knew  the night king already had a good head  start  but that wasn't the biggest issue in  that moment jon also knew that the night  king would not be getting slowed down  like he was  because the whites were obviously all on  the night king's side  that only left jon with minutes or maybe  even only seconds to make it through all  of the madness before the night king  reached bran  john knew for every second he was slowed  down that was another second closer the  night king was to finishing his  mission now as jon made his way across  winterfell  he saw his best friend samwell being  overran by all the whites  he could see that sam was about to die  but he knew that he could not stop for  even one second to help his friend  john knew in that moment he might have  to sacrifice  everyone in that courtyard if it meant  stopping the night king before he got  bran  every one of the main characters who  were there were fighting off several  wipes during that scene  it looked as if all was about to be lost  jaime lannister was about to die  gendry and berean was about to die even  daenerys who was now no longer on her  dragon  was about to die alongside jorah mormont  in that moment  it seemed as if jon was the only hope  after all he was the only one that was  moving forward  right on the heels of the night king  however if he doesn't make it across  that courtyard  everyone he knew and loved would be dead  all of that was running through jon's  mind in that scene  this is why 